<title>MEXICO: Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to May 17.</title>
<headline>Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to May 17.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Agroindustry Sugar</p>
<p>Committee weekly harvest update for the 1996-1997 (Nov/June)</p>
<p>sugar crop to May 17 (sugar, in tonnes) --</p>
<p>Activity in week May 11-May 17</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97     1,452,402 tns	154,670 tns    10.65 pct</p>
<p>     95-96     1,218,424 tns	140,765 tns    11.55 pct</p>
<p>     94-95     1,532,052 tns	159,240 tns    10.39 pct</p>
<p>Total activity to April 17</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97    38,461,486 tns    4,160,780 tns    10.82 pct</p>
<p>     95-96    38,348,951 tns    4,181,621 tns    10.90 pct</p>
<p>     94-95    36,736,876 tns    3,921,868 tns    10.68 pct</p>
<p>The committee reported that during the week 54 of the country's active 61 mills were in operation compared to 53 in the 1995-1996 harvest and 54 in the 1994-1995 harvest.</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9530))</p>
